    "life": {
      "type": "ha-about-life",
      "settings": {
        "paper": "shopify://shop_images/HA_ABOUT_PAPER_GREY_LIFE_29.jpg",
        "grain": false,
        "eyebrow": "A life across places",
        "label": "Founder",
        "name": "Angela Hartwick",
        "body": "<p>I’m naturally drawn to truly regenerative systems. Building an off-grid home in the Canadian wilderness that relies entirely on natural systems is the foundation of my work.</p><p>I develop concepts and strategies, and guide their practical application from production to storytelling across diverse cultural contexts.</p><p>Hartwick Creative, working in media, and Hartwick Atelier, working in handwoven natural clothing, are crossover ventures. They explore complex narratives of technology and cultural heritage, globalisation and localisation, opportunity and conservation.</p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/HA_ABOUT_COLLAGE_LIFE.png",
        "image_alt": "Photographs laid one over another: Angela beside a motorcycle before a domed palace in Rajasthan, printed cloth behind",
        "show_placeholder_note": true
      }
    },
